"R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7da59c400296d51070dee96d20a0319438ce392bea21850f39a8f6257887b3e8", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:72fa840089557230abf1005dcb7c2098a3cc4ce606ede92a143cc781ce540e5b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1426f1d138c3e83c0d03df52a99c23a3b08a4851b3e2f3359ac31b8ce1cd7b55", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002>, and\n<MATH_0003>,\nbe fpqc-coverings of <MATH_0004>.\nIf <MATH_0005> is a refinement of <MATH_0006>,\nthen the pullback functor\n<MATHSEG_0001>descent data relative to <MATHSEG_0002>descent data relative to <MATHSEG_0003>\nis fully faithful.\nIn particular, the category of schemes over <MATH_0007>\nis identified with a full subcategory of the category\nof descent data relative to any fpqc-covering of <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6e941752360ea8bf06163bf325ffda454f4681ebf88d5264f77f58e1d2c5aad4", "unit_id": "tag:02W0:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02VV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{W} = \\{U_i \\times_S V_j \\to S\\}_{(i, j) \\in I \\times J}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{V}$", "MATH_0005": "$2$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nDD(\\mathcal{V}) \\ar[rd] \\ar[rr] & & DD(\\mathcal{U}) \\ar[ld] \\\\\n& DD(\\mathcal{W}) &\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$DD(\\mathcal{V}) \\to DD(\\mathcal{W})$", "MATH_0008": "$DD(\\mathcal{U}) \\to DD(\\mathcal{W})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fpqc-refinement-coverings-fully-faithful}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-family}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-fpqc-refinement-coverings-fully-faithful}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e16953b3b9d8cbb471c5e02370a4eb010ee5ec8825e0a16dc91d91413e55c2a5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ff3d5a0f40ab7663b3834f03148f93fc5c1a3a7388d786e49e0c1997dbf3ce3d", "source_text": "Consider the fpqc-covering\n<MATH_0001> of <MATH_0002>.\nIt is a refinement of both <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004>.\nHence we have a <MATH_0005>-commutative diagram of functors and categories\n<MATH_0006>\nNotation as in the proof of\nLemma <REF_0001> and\ncommutativity by Lemma <REF_0002> part (3).\nHence clearly it suffices to prove the functors\n<MATH_0007> and\n<MATH_0008> are fully faithful.\nThis follows from\nLemma <REF_0003>\nas desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3962f97bbaf411ad0e408ca3fac525fcf457e1227662d22d09e2c2f381f87758", "unit_id": "tag:02W0:proof"}
